Appendix J: Identification Devices — Formal Conditions

J.1 Purpose

This appendix formalizes the identification devices of Section 9 and states the conditions under which each device identifies the effect of ℐ_eff on the diversity–coordination relationship.

J.2 Instrumental Variable Conditions

Let Z be an instrument for \mathcal{I}_{\text{eff}}. The instrument is valid if:

J1 (Relevance). \text{Cov}(Z, \mathcal{I}_{\text{eff}}) \neq 0. The first-stage F-statistic exceeds 10 (Stock–Yogo weak instrument threshold).

J2 (Exclusion). Z affects K only through \mathcal{I}_{\text{eff}}, not through any other channel.

J3 (Independence). Z is independent of the error term \varepsilon in the outcome equation.

The exclusion restriction is not testable. It must be defended on institutional grounds: the mandate is imposed by an external authority and does not respond to anticipated coordination outcomes.

J.3 Regression Discontinuity Conditions

Let T_i be the running variable (e.g., employment count for the CSRD threshold), and let c be the cutoff. The RD design identifies the effect of ℐ_eff at c under:

J4 (Continuity). The conditional expectation of the potential outcomes is continuous in T at c in the absence of treatment.

J5 (Monotonicity). Units cannot sort across the threshold in a way that manipulates their treatment status.

J5 is tested by the McCrary density test and by covariate balance tests at the threshold.

J.4 Proposition 20 (RD Identification)

Under J4–J5, the RD estimand is the average treatment effect at the cutoff:

\tau_{RD} = \lim_{T \downarrow c} \mathbb{E}[K \mid T] - \lim_{T \uparrow c} \mathbb{E}[K \mid T]

Proof. Standard result in the RD literature (Hahn, Todd & van der Klaauw, 2001; Imbens & Lemieux, 2008). \square

The proposition establishes that the RD design identifies a local average treatment effect at the threshold. The external validity of the estimate is limited to units near the threshold.

J.5 Bandwidth Selection

The bandwidth is selected by the Imbens–Kalyanaraman or Calonico–Cattaneo–Titiunik algorithm, which minimizes the mean squared error of the RD estimator. The bandwidth is reported with sensitivity to alternative bandwidths (half and twice the optimal).

J.6 Operational Consequence

The identification devices are constructions to be developed case by case. No validated instrument for ℐ_eff currently exists. The framework specifies the conditions under which an instrument would be valid, not the instrument itself.

